This product is a free / open-source / local reimplementation inspired by, and
building on ideas from, the following projects. OpenAtlas is an independent work and
is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OAtlas / open-atlas  (github.com/FauvidoTechnologies/open-atlas)  - MIT
  The overall AA-mode workflow, engine/function catalogue naming (methods.yaml),
  and CLI shape are modelled on OAtlas. All paid/key-required backends have been
  replaced with free, keyless, or local substitutes; no upstream code is vendored.

PyBrowserAutomation (PyBA)  (github.com/FauvidoTechnologies/PyBrowserAutomation)  - see upstream
  The browser-automation API surface (Engine.sync_run / generate_code, DFS/BFS idea)
  informed openatlas/browser/engine.py, which is an independent reimplementation whose
  reasoning uses local Ollama rather than any paid LLM.

OpenJarvis  (github.com/open-jarvis/OpenJarvis)  - Apache License 2.0
  The ToolRegistry / BaseTool / ToolSpec / ToolResult registration pattern and the
  agentskills.io SKILL.md frontmatter rules (name <=64 lowercase-hyphen, description
  <=1024 chars) are clean-room reimplementations of concepts from OpenJarvis.

ATLAS (Adaptive Test-time Learning and Autonomous Specialization)
  (github.com/itigges22/ATLAS)  - AGPL-3.0
  The "put intelligence in the system around the model" design of the local
  plan -> execute -> check -> repair loop informed openatlas/reasoning/loop.py.
  This is a clean-room design; no AGPL-licensed code is copied into this MIT project.

ATSMATRIX Agent VisualizeR  (github.com/anyel1to/atsmatrix-agent-visualizeR--ANYEL1TO)  - MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 ATSMATRIX Technologies / anyel1to.
  openatlas/webserver/visualizer/atsmatrix.html is a MODIFIED copy of the upstream
  index.html; its licence is kept in openatlas/webserver/visualizer/LICENSE.ATSMATRIX.
  OpenAtlas changes: loads real investigation data (window.ATLAS_GRAPH) instead of the
  simulated demo; the Google Gemini chat (which required an API key) is replaced by a LOCAL
  Ollama call with no key; the offline fallback shows an honest graph summary instead of
  simulated statistics; demo "verified" badges are hidden over real data; data-node layout,
  labels and theme-aware text were added.

WhatsMyName  (github.com/WebBreacher/WhatsMyName)
  data/wmn-data.json is the WhatsMyName dataset by Micah Hoffman et al., used for
  username enumeration. See the "license" field inside that file for its terms.

Holehe  (github.com/megadose/holehe)  - optional dependency
  Used, when installed, for keyless email/account-existence corroboration.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Wikipedia  (en.wikipedia.org, via the MediaWiki API)
  The knowledge base ("brain") stores article text under CC BY-SA 4.0 (Wikipedia
  contributors). Each stored document keeps its source URL, revision id and licence; answers
  cite them. Redistributing a brain database must follow CC BY-SA 4.0.

Python dependencies added in v2: FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3), httpx (BSD-3),
phonenumbers (Apache-2.0), psutil (BSD-3); optional ddgs (MIT), holehe (GPL-3.0, installed
separately by the user, not bundled).
